identity:
  id: eravos.reese-bass ; label: Reese Bass ; icon: 🔈 ; accent: "#ff2266"
  comp_intent: >
    Drum & bass / neuro Reese: detuned saw stack whose movement
    comes from phase drift, a swept comb (neuro flange) and slow
    filter drift — sustained, legato, huge.
  novelty: >
    Only organism with a feedback comb-filter stage and stereo
    mid/side width control; the movement is the instrument.

engine:
  graph:
    osc stack: 2..6 saws, symmetric detune (cents), random start phase per note
    → M/S width: mid = sum, side = L−R of voice pairs panned ±width
    → 24 dB LP (cascaded biquads) with filter env + drift LFO (0.05..2 Hz, random-walk smoothed)
    → COMB: DelayNode (1..12 ms) with feedback (−0.95..0.95), delay time swept by comb LFO → neuro flange
    → distortion (asymmetric waveshaper, 4× oversample)
    → sub sine (mono, pre-width, bypasses comb) summed
    → amp → out
  legato: monophonic, glide on overlapping notes
  sub: always mono (low-end safety), level independent

config:
  voices 2..6 def 4 ; detune 0..50 c def 14 ; width 0..1 def 0.7
  cutoff 40..6000 def 500 ; res 0.5..12 def 1.5 ; envAmt 0..4 oct def 1.5 ; envDecay 0.05..3 def 0.8
  drift 0..1 def 0.3 ; driftRate 0.05..2 def 0.2
  combTime 1..12 ms def 4 ; combFb −0.95..0.95 def 0.6 ; combRate: div or Hz (sync toggle) def 1/2 ; combMix 0..1 def 0.4
  dist 0..1 def 0.35 ; sub 0..1 def 0.5 ; glide 0..0.5 def 0.08 ; attack/release

hooks:
  - reese.hook.audio_out   STD.audio_out
  - reese.hook.note_in     STD.note_in
  - reese.hook.midi_in     STD.midi_in
  - reese.hook.transport_in STD.transport_in (comb sync)
  - reese.hook.mod_cutoff  STD.mod_in(cutoff) → detune ±4800 c
  - reese.hook.mod_comb    STD.mod_in(combTime) → delayTime (range 0.001..0.012)
  - reese.hook.mod_width   STD.mod_in(width)

presets: [Classic Reese, Neuro Flange, Wide Rumble, Hoover-ish, Sub Only]

ui:
  hero: stereo field display — goniometer (L/R Lissajous) from real analyser pair showing width + drift
  panels: STACK (voices, detune, width) | FILTER | COMB (visualised notch comb over spectrum) | DRIVE+SUB
  ui_hooks: standard_ui_hooks

tests:
  - standard_tests
  - width 0 → L == R (correlation > 0.999); width 1 → correlation < 0.6
  - sub stays mono at width 1
  - comb feedback 0.95 stable (no runaway: peak < 0 dBFS over 10 s)
  - legato overlapping notes: single amp envelope

